   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Imperfective gerund",
     "texto": [
      "The imperfective gerund expresses an action happening at the same time as the main verb. It is formed from the present stem with **-а/-я**; the 3rd person plural helps to recognise the stem: **читают → чита- → читая**, **слушают → слуша- → слушая**, **работают → работа- → работая**. There are exceptions and changes in the root.",
      "In the usual construction, the subject of the gerund is the same as the subject of the main verb: **Читая книгу, я пью чай** («Reading a book, I drink tea»: I read and I drink tea).",
      "Posture forms such as **сидя** («sitting») and **стоя** («standing») can also work as adverbs; here they express a simultaneous action of the same subject."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Perfective gerund",
     "texto": [
      "The perfective gerund expresses an action that happens before the main one. The endings **-в** and **-вши** are common: **написать → написав**, **вернуться → вернувшись**; some roots have special forms, such as **прийти → придя**.",
      "Here too the subject must match: **Придя домой, я обедаю** («On arriving home, I have lunch»: I arrive and I have lunch). Avoid sentences where it seems that someone else does the gerund."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
